WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.730
- [Kelly Clarkson] So
Will Smith plays your Dad.

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.920
Was that crazy?

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.400
Like, were you nervous to meet him?

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.233
- [Both] Yeah.

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:07.066
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:07.066 --> 00:00:08.787
- I love that every
answer will be in unison.

00:00:08.787 --> 00:00:09.980
(all laugh)

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:10.813
- [Demi Singleton] I know.

00:00:10.813 --> 00:00:12.560
That's just how we naturally talk now

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.393
when we're together.

00:00:13.393 --> 00:00:15.570
But yeah, I was definitely nervous

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:16.750
meeting Mr. Will.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.955
He's the "Fresh Prince
of Bel-Air", you know.

00:00:18.955 --> 00:00:19.788
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:00:19.788 --> 00:00:20.621
- I grew up wa--

00:00:20.621 --> 00:00:21.454
(audience laughs)

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.287
- [Kelly Clarkson]
Philadelphia, born and raised.

00:00:22.287 --> 00:00:23.120
- [Both] Right?

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:23.953
- On the playground.

00:00:23.953 --> 00:00:25.120
- [Both] Where you spent most of the days.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.895
- Yeah. Crazy. It's crazy.

00:00:26.895 --> 00:00:28.220
No, it is a crazy thing,

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.410
and he's done so many films

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:31.480
and he's had just such an amazing career.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.920
I just can't imagine being so young

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:33.753
and then being arou--

00:00:33.753 --> 00:00:34.586
or even my age,

00:00:34.586 --> 00:00:35.527
being around someone
like that and being like,

00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:37.107
"Oh my God, you've done
so many amazing things".

00:00:37.107 --> 00:00:38.127
"You're such a great actor."

00:00:38.127 --> 00:00:39.900
- I mean, he's pretty phenomenal.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:40.733
- [Saniyya Sidney] No, yeah.

00:00:40.733 --> 00:00:41.970
- Just like you said, despite,

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:42.950
he had so much success,

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.456
but despite that he's so humble.

00:00:44.456 --> 00:00:46.239
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah
he seems genuinely cool.

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:47.072
- And so,

00:00:47.072 --> 00:00:47.920
kind, you know.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.753
When you speak to him,

00:00:48.753 --> 00:00:50.475
it's just like speaking
to any normal person.

00:00:50.475 --> 00:00:51.463
[Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:00:51.463 --> 00:00:52.296
- That's what people really love.

00:00:52.296 --> 00:00:53.190
- And he has the best shoe game.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.023
- [Kelly Clarkson] Best shoe game?

00:00:54.023 --> 00:00:56.020
- The best shoe game I've
ever seen in like ever.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.390
- Shoe game as in like Nike's?

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.330
Like that kinda, like
sneakers? I love sneakers.

00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.163
- I mean, it's like,

00:00:59.163 --> 00:00:59.996
Nike's.

00:00:59.996 --> 00:01:01.274
It's like Air Jordan Ones.

00:01:01.274 --> 00:01:03.190
And he doesn't tie his shoes.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:04.070
Like that's his thing.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:04.903
[Kelly Clarkson] What?

00:01:04.903 --> 00:01:06.000
- He doesn't tie his
shoes. He doesn't want to.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.940
- That's just like trying
to break your ankle.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.530
(laughing)

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:11.290
That's just dangerous is what that is.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.210
I love sneakers.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.620
That's my whole closet.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.450
This is not what I looked
like in my off time.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.628
(laughing)

00:01:16.628 --> 00:01:18.909
This is not-- this is all fake news.

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:20.270
(audience laughing)

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.750
So how you-- gotta be honest with me,

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.360
like how we're Will Smith's tennis skills?

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.590
Like, oh.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:26.470
Your eyes.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:28.710
(laughing)

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:29.543
You were like,

00:01:29.543 --> 00:01:30.530
so.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:31.870
Wait. Don't, y'all usually have to,

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.460
for films, have to like
really go hardcore?

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.310
And like practice for what you're doing?

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:37.460
Oh, so y'all did. He didn't?

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:38.614
- So we did. We did some--

00:01:38.614 --> 00:01:41.950
we did some very intense tennis training,

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.030
but Mr. Will did not.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.371
And that's mostly because

00:01:44.371 --> 00:01:46.470
Richard didn't play.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:47.550
He didn't know how to play tennis.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.060
He kind of taught himself

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.810
in order to teach Serena and Venus.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.643
- [Kelly Clarkson] Oh.

00:01:51.643 --> 00:01:52.810
- [Demi Singleton] He
had really no experience

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:53.850
with the sport until

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.680
he decided that he felt that would be best

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.180
for his girls.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.618
So Mr. Will did not
train as much as we did.

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:01.868
(laughing)

00:02:02.824 --> 00:02:03.990
- It's still respectful

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.024
'cause you're calling him Mr. Will.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:05.857
- Yeah.

00:02:05.857 --> 00:02:06.690
(laughing)

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.540
That's awesome. It's nice. It's nice.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:10.580
- Yeah, it was a lot
of fun playing with him

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.690
because I feel like it made
us feel like we were so good

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:14.881
because you know,

00:02:14.881 --> 00:02:17.498
(laughing)

00:02:17.498 --> 00:02:18.331
(crowd applause)

00:02:18.331 --> 00:02:20.271
- You can't hear that enough.

